<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/hooks/on-start', '/app/create-app']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/stop.test.ts',
            from: ["test('SIGTERM stops the app through onStop and exits 0"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/stop.test.ts',
            from: ["test('App.stop asked twice runs onStop once"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Close the database pool after the last request">
        <p>The hook runs once the app stops taking requests and those in flight have drained,
            so the pool outlives every one of them. <code>await stop()</code> runs the hooks
            filed after yours first. The hook runs on <code>SIGTERM</code>, <code>Ctrl-C</code>
            and quitting the native app, where a <code>process.on('SIGTERM')</code> never runs.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script server>
            import { onStop } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import { pool } from './lib/pool.server.ts'

            onStop(async (stop) => {
                await stop()
                await pool.close()
            })
            </script>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Run every teardown hook when a test ends">
        <p>Hold the app with <code>await using</code>. The block's end calls
            <code>App.stop</code>, a failed test included, and the suite does not hang on an
            open pool.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { expect, test } from 'bun:test'
            import { createApp } from '@abide/abide/server'

            test('the pool answers', async () => {
                await using app = await createApp()
                const answer = await app.fetch(new Request('http://crm/ops/getPool'))
                expect(answer.status).toBe(200)
            })
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
